PKG=grep
NAME=GNU grep 2.5.1a - recursive/color grep
ARCH=Amiga
VERSION=2.5.1a-2
CATEGORY=utility
CLASSES=none
VENDOR=amix-packages
# Authored PSTAMP -- an unset one leaks the build host into a distributed file.
PSTAMP=amix-packages-grep-2.5.1a-2
# Coexists with stock: stock SVR4 grep is /usr/bin/grep -> /sbin/grep, which this
# package does NOT touch.  Ours is /opt/amix/bin/grep and wins by PATH, adding
# recursive -r, -o, --color, a reliable -E, and its own bundled GNU regex over
# the feature-poor stock tool.
DESC=GNU grep 2.5.1a with recursive -r, -o, --color and reliable -E over stock SVR4 grep, which it does NOT replace (stock /usr/bin/grep is untouched; ours wins by PATH). Installs /opt/amix/bin/{grep,egrep,fgrep}. Carries its own GNU regex; strcasecmp comes from libacompat, statically linked. Add /opt/amix/bin to PATH to use it.
